+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failed constraint, and the executor is not called; valid input passes through unchanged, including unlisted properties. ([validated by: rejects missing required input before executing and passes valid extra keys unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L12))
+
+Static schemas compile at registration, and function-valued definitions resolve and validate against the schema returned for each call. ([validated by: uses the schema resolved for each function-valued definition call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49)) ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema during registration and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L71))
